# soft target. Its worst case is about 1.85 GiB of anonymous memory: a full 1 GiB heap (no run reached it) plus the
# most measured beside the heap, 869 MiB (package 41's REVIEW-3, finding 1), which nothing caps. So 2560M acts only
# on something abnormal; 1100M throttled the game into swap. The heap values and
# JVM_ARGS reach a new instance only (provision): one that already exists keeps the values it was created with.
